			<div class="content" id="post-content-4809988">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Genre (Optional): Unsure</p>
<p>Page Layout (Optional):</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: A Foundation raid on an AWCY exhibition results in a strangely built 'computer' coming into containment. It is similar to Google but shows results from any dimension in the multiverse.</p>
<p>Central Narrative: The meat of the article is in the test logs, as anything searched produces an endless number of results, providing the Foundation with knowledge of other dimensions. Then one test shows no results. Given that keyboard spam still gave results, what is the one thing that doesn't exist in any dimension?</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: The Foundation has to try and replicate the result to determine if it poses any threat, becoming more frantic as time goes on, with the Foundation pumping more and more resources into it to solve the mystery.</p>
<p>Additional Notes: I have partly-fleshed out plans for a minor tale series following the mysterious result-less thing, but I won't work on that until this idea does well as an article, if it doesn't then I'll shelve it for a while.</p>

