<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">[Placeholder]</span></p>
<p>I don't really see why the anomaly should be in AWCY's hands in the first place? There seems to be no connection apart from, &quot;Oh, we found it there&quot;, so I think you can do away with that origin story. Other than that, I feel like the article will get really repetitive if it is just test logs without a solid goal in mind. You tried to introduce tension by introducing a search query that gives nothing, but if it gives nothing, then it simply doesn't exist in the multiverse? Why does Foundation have to care about that? Why would Foundation pump so many resources when they can just keep typing the same query in to give the same result that it simply doesn't exist? What's so frightening about it that would make Foundation so panicked?</p>
<p>Wikidot PM me when you answered the questions in your reply.</p>

