			<div class="content" id="post-content-4812286">
									

<p>Thanks for the reply.</p>
<p>The AWCY was just a simple origin story, explaining (vaguely) that it was made for an AWCY exhibition, that can be done away with easily with no problems.</p>
<p>There is a goal in mind for the test logs. I didn't have the space for it in the first post, and I got sidetracked by IRL stuff so I didn't make another post, but it goes like this:</p>
<p>Long ago, elder gods, cosmic entities, etc. One god gets too ambitious, and is erased from reality, showing the power of these beings. A few eons later, the last remaining god, who was suspicious that the erased god was never actually erased but managed to escape, finds the Computer in the Foundation. Using some elder-god mind magic, he gains access to the computer as a d-class, specifically the second one. After a few searches, the god finds the one that confirms that the god was indeed erased, and kills himself using the computer. (Explanation later)</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This is all told from the Foundation's view, and they know nothing. They see some D-class turn up out of nowhere just as the first dies, and somehow survives the computer, and searches his own things, and get worried. They don't know what was searched to give no results, so they want to find that search to work out if this absence of a thing is a problem or not.</p>
<p>With luck, I will make a tale on the perspective of the erased god and the god in the Foundation, showing what actually happened (mostly) and that the god was indeed erased. But nature abhors a vacuum, so a new god of the same power as the old one is made to fill that hole. He has no memory and no idea what or who he is.</p>
<p>From here I could go anywhere: tales following this god trying to find who he is, SCP articles of anomalies caused by the unknowable power in this entity, but I can't make the God himself an SCP without tweaking it a lot.</p>
<p>Now the reason the computer is deadly: Data transmission. We communicate through sight and hearing and touch, but what if another dimension has a sense called 'Snorf', where they pick up electric signals to communicate? A website for them would just blast out a wave of electricity, which would be very dangerous to be in. Because of this it keeps the logs unique every time, as it's a gamble whether or not its going to kill someone. The Foundation views D-Class as disposable anyway, so they'll throw a few at this computer until they can answer questions like &quot;How to physics for Fleebians&quot; or something, as the knowledge of the multiverse is worth a few casualties.</p>
<p>So from Elder Gods to Snorf-blasts and Fleebians, I hope that answered your questions. If you have any more, please let me know.</p>
</div>
