<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">[Placeholder, expect reply in less than 2 days.]</span></p>
<p>I'm going to give some advice here. Don't plan any tales yet. Write the complete story out in this one SCP article that you're pitching to me, which is your first. Right now, this pitch doesn't deserve multiple derivative tales because it can be a neat anecdote.</p>
<p>In your new idea, you've introduced a lot of stuff that I'm going to try to break down.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This is all told from the Foundation's view, and they know nothing.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So how are the readers supposed to be interested in this story if they are kept in the dark too? If you don't answer any questions and the events are introduced in a seemingly-random manner, like the DClass appearing out of no where, how are readers supposed to connect the dots and deduce that a god is investigating a bureaucratic mishap? By leaving all these answers to be written in a tale later, that's lazy, and you should just focus on how you want to explain this story through this article first, so that readers will be interested enough to even read your next few works.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Because of this it keeps the logs unique every time, as it's a gamble whether or not its going to kill someone.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Please do specify what electric waves are, I don't think electricity can travel through the air unless particles are ionised, and for that to happen, it requires the energy of a lightning strike. That will ultimately transform it into another anomaly altogether, into &quot;The computer that calls Thor's mighty thunder every time someone performs a search on it&quot;. I kid, of course, but please do clarify.</p>
<p>Also, you said that a website for another dimension produces these lethal waves every time, so why would it be a gamble for the Foundation? It is literally confirmed they will die, and death without reason isn't really a tense thing anymore. So if these DClass keep dying, what is Foundation supposed to learn about the multiverse?</p>

