<p>I understand planning tales already is ambitious, and I will try to fit all the story into this one article.</p>
<p>Also, I feel a little clarification is in order:</p>
<p>The electric waves was an example of what <em>might</em> happen if you use it. There are infinite multiverses and therefore infinite methods of communication, and while an infinite amount would be readable to us, and infinite amount would not, and an infinite amount would kill us.</p>
<p>The reason it's a gamble is because the Foundation doesn't know what will happen if you click a link, it could:</p>
<ul>
<li>be normal english</li>
<li>be written in a hybrid of french and russian</li>
<li>fire a giant laser</li>
<li>emit a toxic cloud</li>
<li>give you AIDS</li>
<li>download a virus</li>
</ul>
<p>And that's where the test logs would shine: a list of random events that happen when something is searched.</p>
<p>Obviously if you go to &quot;free-money-no-virus.lep.ha&quot; (.lep.ha being an example of otherdimensional websites) and it summons a single gerbil, if you go back to that same website it will summon another gerbil. The effects are based on the equivalent of the .com, so eventually the Foundation could learn what each website will do.</p>

