<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Throughout the logs, a D-Class will be making additional searches, outside the requested ones. The Foundation, wanting to get as much interdimensional info as possible, let's this continue for now.</p>
<p>Eventually, the D-Class only makes his own searches, and he is interviewed to find out why he's not doing what he should be doing.</p>
<p>Long expositional tale short he says there was a group of ten, and one got a bit too aggressive. He ended up taking out seven members of the group before he himself fell, and after seeing the deaths of 80% of his friends, one offed himself, leaving one. This one, the D-Class, believes the aggressive one survived and is using the computer to find out.</p>
<p>All ten of them were elder gods. (No part in the article mentions gods, so a potential name for the article is 'A Tale of Ten Gods'. I have seen other SCPs do this, and there is only one group of ten in the article)</p>
<p>The interviewer does something very uncharacteristic, indicating elder god mind-magic, and the D-Class is permitted to keep searching for the aggressive god.</p>
<p>The D-Class searches for one more thing, but the search term isn't recorded, as the D-Class, satisfied with the lack of results from the final search, looks up one more random thing, causing a massive electric shockwave that kills all personnel present save one, including the god, corrupts the camera footage and causes immense structural damaged to the room.</p>
<p>The Foundation is obviously concerned at a lack of results as mentioned by the survivor, but they don't know what was searched.</p>
</div>
